---
import BaseHead from "../components/BaseHead.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import ExternalLink from "../components/ExternalLink.astro";
// import { Image } from "astro:assets";
// import imgFirstSetup from "../assets/timeline/2016-02-08_first_setup.webp";
// import imgSecondSetup from "../assets/timeline/2019-05-23_second_setup.webp";
// import imgThirdSetup from "../assets/timeline/2021-08-07_third_setup.webp";
// import img3dGame from "../assets/timeline/2023-02-28_3d_game.webp";
// import imgPortrait from "../assets/timeline/2025-07-26_portrait.webp";
// import imgPcb from "../assets/timeline/2026-02-17_pcb.png";
// import imgGoKart from "../assets/timeline/2026-02-19_go_kart.webp";
// import imgGoKartCockpit from "../assets/timeline/2026-03-05_go_kart_cockpit.webp";
// import imgCircuit from "../assets/timeline/2026-03-06_circuit.svg";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead title="Timeline" description="Technical life of deanqx" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <Header />
    <main>
      <h1>Timeline</h1>
      <img
        src="/timeline/2025-07-26_portrait.webp"
        alt="Portrait of me"
        width={300}
      />
      <p>Hello</p>
      <h2>June 2026</h2>
      <p>Server and this Website</p>
      <div style="position: relative;">
        <h2>February 2026</h2>
        <div class="circuit-background"></div>
        <div class="image-grid">
          <img
            style="grid-row: 1;"
            src="/timeline/2026-03-05_go_kart_cockpit.webp"
            alt="Go-Kart cockpit hardware"
            width={400}
          />
          <img
            style="grid-row: 2;"
            src="/timeline/2026-02-17_pcb.png"
            alt="3D view of a Go-Kart Circuit I designed and built."
            width={400}
          />
          <img
            style="grid-row: span 2;"
            src="/timeline/2026-02-19_go_kart.webp"
            alt="Go-Kart"
            width={400}
          />
        </div>
      </div>
      <p>text</p>
      <ExternalLink href="https://github.com/deanqx/go-kart">
        go-kart
      </ExternalLink>
      <h2>March 2025</h2>
      <video
        src="/timeline/2025-03-07_first_pcb.webm"
        type="video/mp4"
        loading="lazy"
        muted
        autoplay
        loop
        playinline
        width="700"></video>
      <p>text</p>
      <h2>February 2024</h2>
      <video
        src="/timeline/2024-02-03_fluffy.mp4"
        alt="2D Game where you play a cloud and dodge air planes."
        type="video/mp4"
        loading="lazy"
        muted
        autoplay
        loop
        playinline
        width="700"></video>
      <ExternalLink href="https://github.com/deanqx/Fluffy">
        Fluffy
      </ExternalLink>
      <h2>February 2023</h2>
      <img
        src="/timeline/2023-02-28_3d_game.webp"
        alt="Working on a 3D Game"
        width={700}
      />
      <ExternalLink href="https://github.com/deanqx/Shadow-Intruder">
        Shadow-Intruder
      </ExternalLink>
      <h2>August 2021</h2>
      <img
        src="/timeline/2021-08-07_third_setup.webp"
        alt="Third computer setup"
        width={700}
      />
      New equipment and new projects. I loved and still love the YouTube Videos about
      AI learning to play a game. So I wanted to learn how AI works. But I didn't
      wanted to just use an existing library -- I wanted to know it worked behind
      the scenes. After all this wasn't a project that needed to be deployed. Note
      that I started it before the AI hype with the ChatGPT 3 release in 2022. At
      this time I also learned about Git and GitHub. So I built the C++ library called
      <ExternalLink href="https://github.com/deanqx/Seayon">Seayon</ExternalLink
      > only following the YouTube series of <ExternalLink
        href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aircAruvnKk&list=PLZHQObOWTQDNU6R1_67000Dx_ZCJB-3pi"
        >3Blue1Brown on Neural Networks</ExternalLink
      >. My goal was to use it as a trading AI. Spoiler: you can't beat
      Wallstreet with a plain Neural Network. In the end I still learned a lot
      and improved my math grades.
      <h2>June 2019</h2>
      <img
        src="/timeline/2019-05-23_second_setup.webp"
        alt="Second computer setup"
        width={500}
      />
      <p>
        The Minecraft server wasn't really as popular as I hoped, so I abandoned
        the server as well as my YouTube Channel in 2018. Surprisingly a few
        friends actually starting playing a lot on it in 2020 when I already
        lost the interest. In 2019 I got an actual desk and started learning
        about Java, C# and Desktop App development. I liked the idea of
        cryptocurrency so I built a digital bank (<ExternalLink
          href="https://github.com/deanqx/BankDemo"
          >BankDemo at GitHub
        </ExternalLink>) with a Server-Client system without encryption. The
        tutorial I followed was about a chat program using Java. After that I
        wanted to look into C# which I did by building a Steam clone (<ExternalLink
          href="https://github.com/deanqx/ArcadeHub"
        >
          ArcadeHub at GitHub
        </ExternalLink>).
      </p>
      <h2>2017</h2>
      <p>
        Published a <ExternalLink
          href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pCqS7dqVr1Q"
          >YouTube video</ExternalLink
        > about the Minecraft server. I was 12 years old at this point.
      </p>
      <h2>February 2016</h2>
      <img
        src="/timeline/2016-02-08_first_setup.webp"
        alt="First computer setup"
        width={500}
      />
      <p>
        Starting from 2014, I was a big Minecraft fan. About 2016 came the idea
        to build my own Minecraft server. My advantage was that my fathers runs
        a technical company and had a Windows server for me to use.
      </p>
      <h2>before 2016</h2>
      <p>
        My first contact with things outside the normal user space started with
        a video on YouTube about "hacking" a Wifi password with the Windows
        command line. It wasn't about actual hacking but rather reading the
        password of the stored Wifis. Afterall that didn't really matter because
        it successfully showed me my Wifi password and I was convinced
        <code>cmd.exe</code> was some kind of hacker tool. I wanted to learn more
        so I searched on YouTube and found this series: <ExternalLink
          href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CvNvUlQ6Knw"
        >
          CMD Tutorial Deutsch von ANSPictures (2010)
        </ExternalLink>
      </p>
      <h2>November 2014</h2>
      <p>
        Start of YouTube Channel: Recorded gaming videos with Phone and later
        learned about on system recording with OBS.
      </p>

      <p>12/2024 - 01/2025 web-login-demo</p>
      <p>06/2024 - 11/2024 Webapp für ein Altenheim:</p>
      <p>
        06/2023 – 06/2024 Server-Auslastungs-Tool: Entwicklung eines internen
        Tools zur Limitierung und Überwachung der Serverlast.
      </p>
      <p>
        12/2020 – 01/2021 Android-App für eine Metzgerei: Ermöglicht Kunden,
        Informationen zu einem Produkt einzusehen.
      </p>
      <p>08/2020 – 05/2023 Seayon</p>
      <p>06/2024 – heute KOWATSCH it-Service</p>
      <p>10/2020 – 05/2021 Thalmaier Logistik und EDV</p>
    </main>
    <Footer />

    <style>
      main {
        max-width: 1024px;
      }

      .circuit-background {
        mask-image: url("/timeline/2026-03-06_circuit.svg");
        mask-size: contain;
        mask-position: top;
        mask-repeat: no-repeat;
        background-color: currentcolor;
        position: absolute;
        inset: 0;
        z-index: -1;
        margin-top: 1lh;
      }

      .image-grid {
        margin-top: 5em;
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
        justify-items: center;
        gap: 2em;
      }

      .image-grid img {
        height: 100%;
      }

      @media (width <= 720px) {
        .image-grid {
          grid-template-columns: 1fr;
          gap: 0.5em;
        }
      }
    </style>
  </body>
</html>
